1
00:00:00,299 --> 00:00:04,651
For an appliance update, first check the installed build and the exact trusted

2
00:00:04,651 --> 00:00:06,584
package supplied by the maintainer.

3
00:00:06,784 --> 00:00:10,808
A source commit, update ZIP and running image are different states.

4
00:00:11,008 --> 00:00:13,339
Finish or reconcile active automation.

5
00:00:13,424 --> 00:00:17,896
Keep a verified database and data backup pair, the previous application image

6
00:00:17,989 --> 00:00:19,162
and a recovery method.

7
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:23,614
Open Appliance Ops, Updates, and Review Storage Before Upload.

8
00:00:23,707 --> 00:00:26,374
Several locations may share the same filesystem.

9
00:00:26,583 --> 00:00:30,522
Keep enough space for the package, image load and backup allowance.

10
00:00:30,765 --> 00:00:33,978
Use reviewed cleanup or the disk expansion guide if needed;

11
00:00:34,135 --> 00:00:38,387
do not delete Docker volumes or the only verified backup to force readiness.

12
00:00:38,764 --> 00:00:43,158
Upload the complete offline ZIP and verify it, then select the imported

13
00:00:43,158 --> 00:00:44,900
package and Check Readiness.

14
00:00:45,078 --> 00:00:47,396
Import validates and stages content;

15
00:00:47,510 --> 00:00:51,714
it does not activate the image or execute a bundled host installer.

16
00:00:51,795 --> 00:00:55,883
If the host service is absent, follow the separate reviewed bootstrap instructions

17
00:00:56,019 --> 00:01:00,278
first. After readiness passes, review and enter the exact version

18
00:01:00,328 --> 00:01:02,461
confirmation. Submit once.

19
00:01:02,733 --> 00:01:06,957
Completed stages are green, the current stage is distinct, and failures

20
00:01:06,957 --> 00:01:11,522
identify their stage. If the browser loses contact, recover the existing

21
00:01:11,522 --> 00:01:14,053
operation rather than starting another installation.

22
00:01:14,402 --> 00:01:18,541
Verify the running image and health build identity, then check retained

23
00:01:18,541 --> 00:01:22,714
credentials, configurations, pipelines, approvals and recovery

24
00:01:22,765 --> 00:01:27,054
progress. If rollback is required, use the recorded previous image

25
00:01:27,190 --> 00:01:30,851
and matching verified backup pair through the documented recovery path.

26
00:01:31,030 --> 00:01:35,236
Appliance rollback does not undo target changes such as enabled encryption.
